# Browser
# What Bot1's page asks for Dack Fayden, Helping Hand in a game of three: the reveal finds Llanowar Elves and then Elvish
# Mystic, both put onto the battlefield and goaded. "For each of those permanents, choose a different opponent": the first
# question is for the Elves, and the page says so - the player chosen gains control of Llanowar Elves, not of "this
# artifact" (Wishclaw Talisman's question). Bot1 chooses Bot2; the Mystic, the second, goes to Bot3, the one opponent left,
# with no question asked. In a game of more than two the player who goes first draws on turn 1 (CR 103.8c).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Dack Fayden, Helping Hand
Island
Island
Forest
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Island
Elvish Mystic
Island x9

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Bot3 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dack Fayden, Helping Hand.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Dack Fayden, Helping Hand: choose an opponent
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Detail = The player you choose gains control of Llanowar Elves
Bot1.ChoosePlayer(Bot2)
! Bot1.ChoosePlayer
[T2 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Turn = 2
Bot2.Battlefield = Llanowar Elves
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.GoadedBy = Bot1
Bot3.Battlefield = Elvish Mystic
Bot3.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.GoadedBy = Bot1
